First of all, let me just say that I've had both of my two best games
in 3-odd years of occasional playing today.  First one wasn't
especially a YASD, I got overwhelmed on the quest leader level.  But
this was the first time that I'd seen the quest, first I'd seen the
Rogue level, deepest I'd ever gone (dlvl 23) by a good 10 levels.  Got
most of the way through the quest and hit a polymorph trap.  Turned
into a new myself about 2 levels less than I'd been.  Probably
should've turned back at that point, but oh well.

Second one's the irritating one.  Was I think about dlvl 10, just below
the Oracle, about to go up into Sokoban.  Had Excalibur up to +3,
pretty decent kit of armor, AC down around -10 or -11 or so, feeling
pretty good.  Killed a cockatrice, moved on down the hall.  Forgot I
was blind.  And what do we do when we're blind?  Yes, that's right, we
feel around on the ground with our hands.  Which were not in gloves.

DYWYPI.

Apart from the fact that I just did a dumb thing, I feel like I've made
a bit of a breakthrough, though.  After a long time of not going about
things especially well, I've figured out some of the things that I need
to do to take it to the next level.  Like the value of backtracking,
and donating, and sacrificing until I get an artifact, etc, etc.
Certainly makes life easier.

